{
  "title": "Senior's toolkit: debugging a live cluster",
  "summary": "The commands for each symptom: events, describe, logs -p, debug, port-forward, jsonpath, wait and diff.",
  "minutes": 6,
  "kind": "lesson",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Senior's toolkit: debugging a live cluster",
      "body": "Symptom first, then the one command that explains it. Everything here is read-only except `debug`, which only adds a container.",
      "toolkit": [
        {
          "cmd": "kubectl get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp",
          "what": "The namespace's timeline: scheduling, pulls, probes, kills, quota rejections.",
          "flags": [
            [
              "--field-selector type=Warning",
              "only problems"
            ],
            [
              "kubectl events --for pod/NAME",
              "one object's events"
            ],
            [
              "-A",
              "every namespace"
            ]
          ],
          "example": "kubectl events -n shop --for deploy/api --types=Warning",
          "lang": "bash"
        },
        {
          "cmd": "kubectl describe pod NAME",
          "what": "Spec, state, last state (exit code, OOMKilled) and the pod's Events.",
          "flags": [
            [
              "-l app=api",
              "every pod with the label"
            ]
          ],
          "example": "kubectl describe pod -l app=api | tail -n 20",
          "lang": "bash"
        },
        {
          "cmd": "kubectl logs POD -p",
          "what": "What the crashed container printed; without `-p` you read the fresh restart.",
          "flags": [
            [
              "-c NAME",
              "pick the container"
            ],
            [
              "--since=10m --timestamps",
              "recent lines, with times"
            ],
            [
              "-l app=api --prefix",
              "all replicas"
            ]
          ],
          "example": "kubectl logs deploy/api -p --tail=50",
          "when": "CrashLoopBackOff",
          "lang": "bash"
        },
        {
          "cmd": "kubectl debug -it POD --image=busybox:1.37 --target=CTR",
          "what": "An ephemeral container with your tools, sharing the app's processes. For images with no shell.",
          "flags": [
            [
              "--copy-to=NAME",
              "debug a copy instead (change command, image)"
            ],
            [
              "node/NAME",
              "a shell on the node"
            ]
          ],
          "example": "kubectl debug -it api-7d9f8 --image=busybox:1.37 --target=api -- sh",
          "lang": "bash"
        },
        {
          "cmd": "kubectl port-forward svc/NAME 8080:80",
          "what": "Reach a ClusterIP Service from your machine without exposing it.",
          "flags": [
            [
              "-n NS",
              "namespace"
            ],
            [
              "--address 127.0.0.1",
              "bind only to loopback (the default)"
            ]
          ],
          "example": "kubectl port-forward -n payments svc/ledger 8081:80 &",
          "lang": "bash"
        },
        {
          "cmd": "kubectl get ... -o jsonpath='{...}'",
          "what": "Exactly the fields you need, scriptable. `custom-columns` for tables.",
          "flags": [
            [
              "{range .items[*]}...{end}",
              "one line per item"
            ],
            [
              "--sort-by=.lastTimestamp",
              "order by any field"
            ],
            [
              "-L app -w",
              "label column, watch"
            ]
          ],
          "example": "kubectl get pods -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name} {.status.containerStatuses[0].lastState.terminated.reason}{\"\\n\"}{end}'",
          "lang": "bash"
        },
        {
          "cmd": "kubectl wait --for=condition=Available deploy/NAME",
          "what": "Block until a condition holds; fail at the timeout. Replaces sleep loops.",
          "flags": [
            [
              "--for=jsonpath='{...}'=VALUE",
              "any field"
            ],
            [
              "--for=delete",
              "until it is gone"
            ],
            [
              "--timeout=60s",
              "give up"
            ]
          ],
          "example": "kubectl wait -n shop --for=condition=Available deploy/api --timeout=120s",
          "lang": "bash"
        },
        {
          "cmd": "kubectl diff -f DIR",
          "what": "What an apply would change, computed by the API server. Exit 1 when different.",
          "flags": [
            [
              "--server-side",
              "with server-side apply semantics"
            ],
            [
              "-k DIR",
              "a Kustomize overlay"
            ]
          ],
          "example": "kubectl diff -k overlays/prod",
          "lang": "bash"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "`kubectl get pods` shows `Running` and `READY 0/1`. Which command tells you why?",
      "options": [
        "`kubectl describe pod NAME` (look for `Unhealthy` readiness events)",
        "`kubectl logs NAME -p`",
        "`kubectl get nodes`",
        "`kubectl diff -f .`"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Running but not Ready means the readiness probe fails; the kubelet records each failure as an `Unhealthy` event with the probe's error. `logs -p` is for crashes, and this container has not crashed."
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Read what the crashed `api` container printed, the last 50 lines.",
      "code": "kubectl __1__ deploy/api __2__ --tail=50",
      "blanks": [
        "logs",
        "--previous"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "describe",
        "--follow",
        "exec"
      ],
      "explain": "`--previous` (`-p`) reads the last terminated container of each pod container; `--tail` limits the output."
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "prompt": "Read-only, or does it change the cluster?",
      "buckets": [
        "Read-only",
        "Changes the cluster"
      ],
      "items": [
        [
          "`kubectl get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`kubectl diff -f k8s/`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`kubectl wait --for=condition=Available deploy/api`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`kubectl debug -it api-x --image=busybox:1.37`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`kubectl rollout undo deploy/api`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`kubectl logs -p api-x`",
          0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Make it a habit",
      "body": [
        "Symptom, then events and `describe`, then `logs -p` or `debug`. Ask with `jsonpath`, wait with `wait`, change with `diff` first. The boss of this module is a night on call with six of these failures at once."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
